From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] overlay: Times New Roman cells get a bundled serif face (Tinos) on the web

Owner request 2026-11-10: Times New Roman everywhere. On the web there are no system fonts, so the serif role of the grid fell back to the sans UI face. The overlay's FONTS list may now carry a third face (office-fallback-serif, Tinos subset, Times New Roman's metric twin); it leads the serif font family behind an installed serif. Only sheets and slides pass the third face.
Test: ui-egui overlay test times_new_roman_cells_resolve_to_the_bundled_serif.
---
 crates/ui-egui/build_office.rs             |  6 +++++-
 crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay.rs       |  6 ++++++
 crates/ui-egui/src/office_overlay_tests.rs | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

